The required utilities for the DAC960 can still be had, yet they are 
difficult to find

The firmware update has never worked for me on the Alpha, better use a 
PC for
that (Make sure to update to v 2.73 and nothing newer, even on dual 
eeprom controllers)

For all the alpha goodies, see

http://h18000.www1.hp.com/support/files/alphant/drivers/index.html

You want this (The configuration utility)

ftp://ftp.compaq.com/pub/softpaq/alphant/m-arcapp.zip

Place it's content on an ms-dos formatted floppy and run from the srm

If you need any help, let me know, either privately or via the list.

For the firmware, see

http://www.lsilogic.com/products/stor_prod/raid/legacy_dac960.html

in particular, you want (x86 binary!)

http://www.lsilogic.com/techlib/marketing_docs/storage_stand_prod/raid/gam/fwpl273.exe

Regards,
Roberto





